Subject: [PATCH] Preserve compatible platforms in transfer pulls

The transfer store uses an ordered list of exact platform matches. Sending
only the CPU-specific host platform skips baseline amd64 manifests on v4
hosts, causing the complete-content check to reject normal ECS image pulls.
Keep the compatibility-vector adapter in daemon/containerd, derived from
containerd/platforms v1.0.0-rc.5 under Apache-2.0. Do not change the vendor
module or add an exported API that a vendor refresh would delete.
Use the vector for download selection and unpack configuration, limiting
selected manifests to one to match Docker's platform preference behavior.

Exercise the transfer store's image filter for fallback, preference,
unsupported platforms and unpack configuration in the package regressions.
These in-process regressions use containerd client 2.4.1; daemon 2.2.9
behavior is separately validated by the live ECS pulls.
---

